experiment: credgate
  SHORT RUN — 600000 ticks against a minimum of 3400000. CAN THE CREATURE TARGET ITS OWN REWARD? credit-oracle settled that the 0.22
  wipe is credit assignment, not a collision: capacity found two lessons
  interfering while driving DISJOINT groups, because node perturbation nudges
  every neuron on one broadcast scalar. A per-neuron mask fixes it (1.03 vs
  0.84) but that is an oracle. This drives the mask from the creature's OWN
  ear-EMA context index, with a coin-flip arm to separate the index CONTENT
  from the mere act of masking. 12 seeds
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  instrument        credgate   trial seed 000000000135e16e   214 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  seed family       offset 904837 -> first creature 000000000142f64e (FRESH)
  what the wipe IS  not a representational collision. `capacity` found two
                    lessons interfering while driving DISJOINT groups, and
                    `credit-oracle` gave the reason: the groups are disjoint,
                    the REWARD is what they share. Node perturbation nudges
                    bias_[i] for EVERY neuron in the module on one broadcast
                    scalar, so teaching B random-walks A's setting.
  the ceiling       a per-neuron reward mask gives retention 1.03 vs 0.84
                    broadcast, at ~30% of the learning rate. But it is an
                    ORACLE: the host knows which lesson is live.
  the question      can the creature's OWN derived context drive that mask?
                    `ema-index` derives a usable context off the ear rate EMA
                    at 16/18; `ctxretain` gated on it and the index never
                    separated (0.23/0.23). The halves have never been joined.
  halves MEASURED   `silences-the-wrong-side`: a LOW target works by
                    suppressing the UPPER half, a HIGH one the LOWER. A is
                    f1 320 and B is 850, so A takes the UPPER and B the LOWER.

  PRE-REGISTERED
    AGREEMENT FIRST, before any retention number is read. `credit_agree` is
      the fraction of trials where the mask landed on the half the LIVE lesson
      wants. oracle must read 100% by construction -- if it does not, the
      mechanism is miswired and nothing else is readable. shuf must sit at
      ~50%. DERIVED IS THE WHOLE QUESTION: at ~50% the index carries nothing
      about which lesson is live and a null retention result says nothing
      about gating, only about this index.
    PRIMARY         the AB-minus-keep gap per mode. oracle should shrink it
                    (that is credit-oracle replicating); derived shrinking it
                    too is the finding.
    SPECIFICITY     `shuf` must NOT shrink it. If a coin flip works as well as
                    the index, what helps is the masking itself -- halving the
                    write -- and not credit assignment at all.
    THE COST        the oracle bought 1.03 at ~30% of the learning rate, so
                    err_taught is expected to DEGRADE under every mask. A gap
                    that closes while err_taught collapses is the `regionband`
                    failure again, and it is refused the same way.

